ttsnoop's _tt_sigset kept to itself.

ttsnoop has its own copy of _tt_sigset, the libtt function that installs a
signal handler that stays installed, and calls it only from its own file.
With a shared libtt the program's copy wins and the clash goes unseen;
linked statically with libtt, whose tt_port.o comes in for other calls, it
is two definitions.  ttsnoop's copy is now static.  (ttsnoop.C.src is the
input dtcodegen merges into ttsnoop.C: README, The App Builder's code.)

--- a/programs/ttsnoop/ttsnoop.C.src
+++ b/programs/ttsnoop/ttsnoop.C.src
@@ -195,7 +195,7 @@
 #define SIG_PF sig_pf_t
 #endif
 
-int
+static int
 _tt_sigset(
 	int     sig,
 	SIG_PF  handler )
